+### 32.2 The tool and the configuration
+
+- **The tool.** `tools/ledger_coverage.py` and `tools/ledger_coverage/` at the tool commit `T`
+  (`<T: full id, on main's first-parent chain>`), landed by `<tool landing PR>`. Its design is
+  `<adopted tool design: version and record>`.
+- **The configuration.** `retirement-config.json` in this directory, schema `oi-retirement-config/1`, `config_id`
+  `a1exit-retirement-config`, version 1. It is read only from `F`'s tree, as
+  `--config F:verification/audits/foundations/a1exit-deletion-20261121/retirement-config.json`. It carries:
+  - `tool`: every file of the tool at `T` (the entry point and every file under `tools/ledger_coverage/`) and the
+    workflow whose runs may produce an acceptable result, each by blob sha256;
+  - `repository_id`: 1156244443;
+  - `records`: every record and review record a run may use, each by `{kind, path, blob_sha256}`. It references no
+    authorization record, and `retirement` holds the name and the accountable Issue only;
+  - the ledger, the edit list and the plan checker, and the profiles `ptr`, `repo`, `register`, `register-caps` and
+    `infinity`, read from this directory at `F`.
+- **Its review.** `review-retirement-config-v1.json` in this directory, by a non-author reviewer, covering every field,
+  `tool.workflow` included.
+- **The pinned workflow.** It runs, in this order and nothing else: the fetch of `F` by its full id, the pre-run pin
+  check against the configuration's `tool.files`, and the entry point with `python3 -I -B`. It receives `F` and the
+  configuration path as inputs and names every action by full commit id. It runs only from `main`, so that `T` is on
+  `main`'s first-parent chain when a check runs.
+- **Pins.** §32.9 lists the configuration and its review record with their sha256. It is the last `Record pins`
+  subsection of this record, so both `preserve_check.py` and the tool read it.
+
+### 32.3 The designation of F
+
+The owner designates `F` and the configuration path together (§A.50 items 2 and 5), after the gate of §32.6 and the
+independent review of the exact candidate head. The designation is quoted, with author, time and comment id, in the
+execution result note under `execution/` and in the landing record of the tool's acceptance result. The tool and the
+checkers do not read it: the tool verifies which plan commit and configuration a run used, and the designation states
+that they are the approved ones.
+
+### 32.4 The checks of §11 as tool commands
+
+Every command below is run only by the pinned workflow, as
+`python3 -I -B tools/ledger_coverage.py <operation> --freeze F --config F:verification/audits/foundations/a1exit-deletion-20261121/retirement-config.json --out <dir> <arguments>`.
+No command takes a plan id, a round id or a pin-table argument. A path written `F:<name>` is a file of this directory
+at `F`, resolved through the configuration. `X` is the execution head, `C` the certified head, `M` `main` as
+resolved before landing and `L` the landing.
+
+| §11 item | Arguments | Expected at a T1′-style `X` |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `execution --scientific-base H --candidate X --ledger F:ledger.json --edits F:edits.json`, and `terms --commit X --profile ptr` | splices PASS; the `ptr` hits PASS by W2's rules and the classification of `papers/GR.md:58`; any other hit REVIEW_REQUIRED |
+| 2 | `record --pin E --record F`, and `coverage --commit X --segment E..H --segment H..X=F:ledger.json --hp F:hp.json --classify <records>` | PASS only with the HP, context and hit records the configuration references |
+| 3 | `execution --delegation <configured contract>`, classes `tex`, `pdf`, `ci` | PASS only with exact-head evidence on `X` from a `push` or `workflow_dispatch` run |
+| 4 | `execution`, class `coverage-ledger`, and class `ci` job `coverage_check` | PASS iff the seven re-affirmed fingerprints equal `tools/proof_census.py` |
+| 5 | `execution`, profiles `register` and `register-caps`, per edit, per step and per splice | PASS |
+| 6 | `execution`, profile `infinity`, per edit, per step and per splice | PASS |
+| 7 | `<OPEN, §32.10 item 1>` | — |
+| 8 | `execution`, subject `mirror` | PASS |
+| 9 | `execution`, conformance of `verification/lean-manuscript-census.json` | PASS |
+| 10 | `execution`, subject `lean`, and class `ci` | PASS |
+| 11 | `terms --commit X --check item11 --final` | PASS only when every line the `repo` profile finds is classified by a reviewed rule or record |
+| 12 | `execution`, subject `pin` at H and at `X`, and class `ci` | PASS |
+| 13 | `execution`, class `sc42` | PASS iff byte-identical |
+| 14 | `execution --scientific-base H --main M --candidate X`, then `--certified C --landing L` before landing | candidate PASS against H; landing per the tool's four-tree rules |
+
+A check passes only under the tool's acceptance predicate: exit status 0, a valid `result.json` with outcome PASS
+recomputed by the outcome checker, admission `"chain"` naming this `F` and this pin table, and a producing run whose
+repository, event, `head_sha` and tool and workflow blobs equal the configuration's pins. The tool's countercontrols for
+each item are part of its preregistered control set, which the configuration pins.
